{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting","id":987763,"title":"How would Fables work in the WoD setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-15T08:28:12-07:00","id":987763,"title":"How would Fables work in the WoD setting?","content":"As of late, I've been delving into the absolutely fantastic comic known as Fables and have been drawing quite a few parallels with WoD gamelines.<br /> <br /> After all, both feature isolated communities of supernatural beings who live beneath the noses of the mundane world engaging in twisted power games of monumental consequence.<br /> <br /> For the uninitiated, the Fables setting can be surmised as such:<br /> <br /> Every character and creature from popular stories and tales of old are real, brought to life by centuries of belief, renown, and veneration. Initially, they existed in separate worlds apart from both the mundane and from each other; free to live out their stories time and time again, but this was not to last.<br /> <br /> In time, a dark empire headed by a mysterious being known as the Adversary arose and rolled over kingdom upon kingdom like an unstoppable wave. Soon, even the most powerful of Fables were forced to flee before the coming horde or die beneath its trampling feet. A great exodus of Fables carried tiny bands of refugees to the one place the Adversary hadn't reached; the mundane world.<br /> Now, they are forced to live in secrecy amongst away from the prying eyes of the &quot;Mundies&quot; (Fable slang for the non-magical) for fear that discovery would bring yet another wave crashing down upon their heads, only this time, with nowhere left to run.<br /> <br /> Trapped between the rock of the encroaching Adversary, whose incursions grow more and more bold by the day, and the hard place of a dreary mundane world, the Fables have nothing left to do but wait; forming tightly knit but fragile communities as they prepare for the coming war.<br /> <br /> My question posed to you is this; how would this setting function as a World of Darkness gameline, both mechanically and in terms of lore?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://67.media.tumblr.com/ee663bd3bc297e37358d1d678ea65083/tumblr_inline_npnyyevfOs1spvqit_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","user":"Tadpoleon","date":". 10-15-2016, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","name":"Tadpoleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12380_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:46:46-07:00","id":987773,"title":"","content":"Sounds like something out of Changeling the Dreaming? I'd use that game, or the Conversion guide, or hack Changeling itself. Something to do with Changeling, though - its pretty much right in the name. &quot;Fables&quot; is pretty much a synonym for &quot;fairy tale&quot; after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:13:29-07:00","id":987783,"title":"","content":"Yeah, &quot;Trapped between the rock of the encroaching Adversary, whose incursions grow more and more bold by the day, and the hard place of a dreary mundane world, the Fables have nothing left to do but wait; forming tightly knit but fragile communities as they prepare for the coming war.&quot; is Changeling the Lost to a T, you just have to replace &quot;Adversary&quot; with &quot;Gentry&quot;. Granted, the Fables' origins are a bit more Dreaming than Lost, but it's still workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:02:47-07:00","id":987804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=987773#post987773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like something out of Changeling the Dreaming? I'd use that game, or the Conversion guide, or hack Changeling itself. Something to do with Changeling, though - its pretty much right in the name. &quot;Fables&quot; is pretty much a synonym for &quot;fairy tale&quot; after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, runs along a lot of the same ideas.<br /> <br /> The difference here is that Fables are created by conscious thought while the Fae are made from the subconscious (if my understanding is correct)<br /> <br /> Whereas the Fae are born from dreams, Fables come from the telling of stories.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I suppose so, but it's sort of a reverse situation, innit?<br /> <br /> In CtL, you're returning home after years away and dealing with what's changed while you were gone. In Fables, the characters have been forced out of their land and forced to cope with a whole new world while simultaneously trying to save it from being corrupted like their last home.<br /> <br /> Additionally, all of their accomplishments, wealth, power, influence, they've achieved over centuries long lifetimes have been wiped away. People who were once kings and heroes are just average joes.<br /> It's why so many Fables just give up and sink into poverty and vice; why bother building yourself back up if you know it could just be taken away again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","user":"Tadpoleon","date":". 10-15-2016, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","name":"Tadpoleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12380_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:24:35-07:00","id":987849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=987773#post987773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like something out of Changeling the Dreaming? I'd use that game, or the Conversion guide, or hack Changeling itself. Something to do with Changeling, though - its pretty much right in the name. &quot;Fables&quot; is pretty much a synonym for &quot;fairy tale&quot; after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or an abyssal phenomenon encroaching on the Astral and forcing astral entities into the material en masse, who then starts to influence mundane events according to their predilections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:37:29-07:00","id":987857,"title":"","content":"As Charlaquin said, Fables is basically Changeling: The Dreaming in comic book form, but as Tadpoleon said, it doesn't adapt so cleanly to Lost. Though I haven't read the book in years, and I have some consternation regarding Willingham's conservative pro-Israel metaphor, I love Fables.<br /> <br /> I'd add a wrinkle to CtL mythology perhaps? The land of the Fair Folk is blighted, and many True Fae on the fringes are forced to emigrate to the land of the mundane. Much like the nobles who fled the Russian Revolution, they're forced to give up huge parts of themselves in the process of fleeing their homeland. For the Fae, this means latching on to the myths the mortals hold to keep a fraction of their power tethered to them. Beings who once held limitless power are now relegated to roles like The Huntsman or Bluebeard. They have to compartmentalize their power into archetypes. What happens when a changeling who was once held at the sadistic mercy of one of these beings learns that their former captor is now vulnerable and living in a rent-controlled conclave in the real world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:14:57-07:00","id":987876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=987857#post987857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Charlaquin said, Fables is basically Changeling: The Dreaming in comic book form, but as Tadpoleon said, it doesn't adapt so cleanly to Lost. Though I haven't read the book in years, and I have some consternation regarding Willingham's conservative pro-Israel metaphor, I love Fables.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that his metaphor, or Bigby's? Because unless Bigby is his confirmed author avatar, I'd say that the scene is more a characterization of Bigby, who is very conservative, subscribing to belief in rule by the strong.<br /> <br /> Or did you mean the whole thing as an Israel metaphor?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd add a wrinkle to CtL mythology perhaps? The land of the Fair Folk is blighted, and many True Fae on the fringes are forced to emigrate to the land of the mundane. Much like the nobles who fled the Russian Revolution, they're forced to give up huge parts of themselves in the process of fleeing their homeland. For the Fae, this means latching on to the myths the mortals hold to keep a fraction of their power tethered to them. Beings who once held limitless power are now relegated to roles like The Huntsman or Bluebeard. They have to compartmentalize their power into archetypes. What happens when a changeling who was once held at the sadistic mercy of one of these beings learns that their former captor is now vulnerable and living in a rent-controlled conclave in the real world? </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but what would push them out?<br /> A powerful being like the God Machine finally pushing through the hedge?<br /> A coup from within?<br /> Encroaching Banality? (If that's not a thing in the new Changeling, forgive me for my lack of knowledge)<br /> <br /> One of the major themes of Fables is a sort of cruel hope; it's almost worse that any Fable who chooses can go back to the Homelands at their leisure, because the temptation and longing are crueler than no possibility of return at all.<br /> Worse still, the Homelands have become a cruel mockery of what they once were, making any return trip more of an emotional burden than a nostalgic comfort.<br /> <br /> Destroying the Dreaming altogether would sort of limit this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just thought of something.<br /> What if we brought back the Seelie and Unseelie courts?<br /> <br /> In Fables, the exodus was caused by a new polity rising up and forcing the Fables out into the Mundy world.<br /> Adding in the Seelie and Unseelie courts could provide a similar political disunity into the Dreaming.<br /> Perhaps the Unseelie finally rose up against the Seelie, tired of being relegated to the least loved seasons or vice versa, with the Seelie courts dreading the Unseelie for their dark natures and mysterious agenda and removing them from the equation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","user":"Tadpoleon","date":". 10-15-2016, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","name":"Tadpoleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12380_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:28:46-07:00","id":987888,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Malus. If you want to play it, Changeling's close enough. If you want to be accurate, more flatly transporting the setting over, Astral beings fleeing an intruder of some sort would fit better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:38:47-07:00","id":987895,"title":"","content":"For me, <b>Fables</b> are all about <b>Changeling: The Lost</b>, but from different than typical perspective. In reality, Fables are Loyalist changelings that adhere to their Homeland as original 'creator and master'. They just do not know that 'Homeland' is collection of True Fae in their Domain form, as their never meet their Actors there - 'Homeland' wanted to create 'Paradise' for this creation made from dreams of humans, not interfering with their lives. But then comes Adversary that is enemy True Fae. Fables must saves themselves by forced return to mundane world, if they did not wanted this. On Earth, once Loyalist start to separate themselves on smaller communities to protect and fight Adversary, basically creating Freehold and 2E Courts system.<br /> <br /> Just see <b>Wolf Among Us</b>, great video game in Fables universe on that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kQmvhdsFIOA\" data-code=\"kQmvhdsFIOA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/kQmvhdsFIOA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It is very dark stuff in here, much more <b>CtL</b> than <b>CtD</b> in feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:18:49-07:00","id":987904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tadpoleon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=987804#post987804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I suppose so, but it's sort of a reverse situation, innit?<br /> <br /> In CtL, you're returning home after years away and dealing with what's changed while you were gone. In Fables, the characters have been forced out of their land and forced to cope with a whole new world while simultaneously trying to save it from being corrupted like their last home.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the backstory is kind of backwards for Lost, which is why I sad that aspect is kind of more Dreaming (full disclosure, I know very, very little about Dreaming). But, the story itself, being caught between the danger of the world they left behind and the mundanity of the world they fled to is spot-on for Lost's themes and mood. To me, that's the more important part than the backstory, because it has a bigger impact on play. If I were to run a Fables-inspired chronicle I'd definitely do it in Lost, and I'd fudge the backstories of both Lost and Fables a bit to reconcile the differences. I think Wyrd is on the right track with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, all of their accomplishments, wealth, power, influence, they've achieved over centuries long lifetimes have been wiped away. People who were once kings and heroes are just average joes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so that's kind of atypical for a Durance in Lost - even when they were wonderful they were still traumatic. By the same token though, even when they were torture they were wondrous. So, what if the Adversary wasn't an alien force? What if it's just how they compartmentalized their Keeper's abuse? Their Keeper cherished them, made them kings, queens, heroes, and champions. But also terrorized them, made them soldiers in a fruitless and eternal war against rival Gentry, punished them mercilessly when they displeased it. And maybe they separated the entity they associate with the abuse from the entity that cherished them, to protect themselves, like an abused partner blames the alcohol instead of the abuser.<br /> <br /> Or, like Wyrd said, maybe they are Loyalists and the Adversary is one of their Keeper'a rivals. That works too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's why so many Fables just give up and sink into poverty and vice; why bother building yourself back up if you know it could just be taken away again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, this is so Lost it hurts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:27:40-07:00","id":987961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=987904#post987904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so that's kind of atypical for a Durance in Lost - even when they were wonderful they were still traumatic. By the same token though, even when they were torture they were wondrous. So, what if the Adversary wasn't an alien force? What if it's just how they compartmentalized their Keeper's abuse? Their Keeper cherished them, made them kings, queens, heroes, and champions. But also terrorized them, made them soldiers in a fruitless and eternal war against rival Gentry, punished them mercilessly when they displeased it. And maybe they separated the entity they associate with the abuse from the entity that cherished them, to protect themselves, like an abused partner blames the alcohol instead of the abuser.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.. I like it, but it's hard to generalize psychology like that. Sure, maybe one or two of them responded that way, but it'd not be uniform enough to form a community.<br /> Plus, that would mean that the whole thing came crumbling once they actually got back to the Dreaming and had a poke about for their little Adversary<br /> <br /> And then there's the matter of what the Adversary really IS, but that's a major spoiler that I'll avoid if you don't want it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, like Wyrd said, maybe they are Loyalists and the Adversary is one of their Keeper'a rivals. That works too. </div> </div> </div>That COULD work, but then that would mean they all come from the same keepers, otherwise why would they join up together?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Man, this is so Lost it hurts. </div> </div> </div>I know, right? 'S why I brought it up in here :P<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, so back to a topic we've been skirting around; why do they take the form of characters out of stories?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8492\" data-vbnamecard=\"8492\">dxanders</a> gave us some reasoning, but if our Fables aren't going to be True Fae we need something else.<br /> <br /> What if the True Fae organized some kind of massive play with their changelings? Only rather than have them merely act out human stories, they were forced to quite literally become them, both physically and mentally.<br /> <br /> Initially, they would only tell stories in closed loops, but as the Fae grew bored of the same tales over and over, they'd start to mix and match different parts; why not have Dorothy visit Wonderland for a change? This would explain why kingdoms in the Homeland were once isolated dimensions and eventually fused together over time.<br /> <br /> Eventually I imagine the Fae would want to get in on the action personally, and this is where everything starts to go wrong.<br /> If you've ever seen the movie Westworld I'd think of the situation similarly to that one; every day the actors are reset from any mental or physical damage so that they don't start to realize that they're repeating the same story.<br /> But there's only so much that can be repressed, and as the Fae started to get more twisted with them, stepping in to derail plots and send everything spiraling down into madness the trauma would start to leave imprints that wouldn't fade away.<br /> <br /> Thus, the &quot;Adversary&quot; is the True Fae themselves. The Fables are convinced that the massive sets the True Fae built for them to act out stories on are truly their ancestral homelands and the Fae who are now stepping in to take active roles in the story are some malevolent alien force come to drive them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","name":"Tadpoleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12380_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T22:26:42-07:00","id":988136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tadpoleon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=987961#post987961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That COULD work, but then that would mean they all come from the same keepers, otherwise why would they join up together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read <b>Equinox Road</b>? This sourcebook have information on True Fae and Arcadia - it's from there I got idea of 'Gentry without personhood' ( called Domain Form ).<br /> <br /> In this book there is also one interesting idea - that True Fae are bounded in to so called Feud - basically a pantheon, like Olympians from Greek's myths. On general it works more like 'constant war and betrayal', but I could see that 'Homeland' is exceptional peaceful Feud, where all Keepers agreed to make paradise-like Durance of their changelings ( from whatever reason they want this experiment to work ). Only, as a Feud, sooner or later comes Quarrel and we end with Adversary to rest of Keepers. And this leads to Fables coming to Earth on masse.<br /> <br /> Thing is that in Feuds, changelings of many different Keepers interact so often, they think of themselves as closest to family in Arcadia. Even if your masters make war between themselves, it does not mean their servants need to be enemies. With 'peaceful Durance' option, it's even more have sense that changelings would cooperate in Arcadia - more, it also points why they regret living Land of Wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-16-2016, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T06:50:19-07:00","id":988228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=988136#post988136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you read <b>Equinox Road</b>? This sourcebook have information on True Fae and Arcadia - it's from there I got idea of 'Gentry without personhood' ( called Domain Form ).<br /> <br /> In this book there is also one interesting idea - that True Fae are bounded in to so called Feud - basically a pantheon, like Olympians from Greek's myths. On general it works more like 'constant war and betrayal', but I could see that 'Homeland' is exceptional peaceful Feud, where all Keepers agreed to make paradise-like Durance of their changelings ( from whatever reason they want this experiment to work ). Only, as a Feud, sooner or later comes Quarrel and we end with Adversary to rest of Keepers. And this leads to Fables coming to Earth on masse.<br /> <br /> Thing is that in Feuds, changelings of many different Keepers interact so often, they think of themselves as closest to family in Arcadia. Even if your masters make war between themselves, it does not mean their servants need to be enemies. With 'peaceful Durance' option, it's even more have sense that changelings would cooperate in Arcadia - more, it also points why they regret living Land of Wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, that is something...<br /> <br /> So one (or more) of the pantheon went rogue and the Fables were forced out for their own safety (the rest of the True Fae staying behind as they could fight one of their own)<br /> I must say that I quite like this, you think along exceptional lines my friend.<br /> <br /> What do you think of my reasoning here on why they have assumed the form of popular characters?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if the True Fae organized some kind of massive play with their changelings? Only rather than have them merely act out human stories, they were forced to quite literally become them, both physically and mentally.<br /> <br /> Initially, they would only tell stories in closed loops, but as the Fae grew bored of the same tales over and over, they'd start to mix and match different parts; why not have Dorothy visit Wonderland for a change? This would explain why kingdoms in the Homeland were once isolated dimensions and eventually fused together over time. </div> </div> </div>This would explain why they all decided to be (mostly) peaceful, in order for this little play to keep going undisturbed and add a further layer to their connection to the homelands; in both mind and body they've been transformed into the characters and truly believe that they ARE them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","name":"Tadpoleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12380_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:02:19-07:00","id":988271,"title":"","content":"Alternate idea, Fables as Goetics driven out of the Astral by a powerful Acamoth.<br /> <br /> The Fables claim people allow them to remain in the mundane world, safe from danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:25:13-07:00","id":988446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=988271#post988271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternate idea, Fables as Goetics driven out of the Astral by a powerful Acamoth.<br /> <br /> The Fables claim people allow them to remain in the mundane world, safe from danger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry my friend, not familiar with Goetics. Would you mind giving me some context and explanation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","name":"Tadpoleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12380_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:32:09-07:00","id":988457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tadpoleon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=988446#post988446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry my friend, not familiar with Goetics. Would you mind giving me some context and explanation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Goetia are basically living representations of thoughts, concepts, and ideas which form in the Astral, and all fictional characters have at least one. Though normally cannot ever leave the astral or claim creatures (which is were the goetia influences a creature enough with it's essence that it can merge with it not only spiritually but also physically resulting a hybrid between the &quot;host&quot; and the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:51:20-07:00","id":988475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=988457#post988457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goetia are basically living representations of thoughts, concepts, and ideas which form in the Astral, and all fictional characters have at least one. Though normally cannot ever leave the astral or claim creatures (which is were the goetia influences a creature enough with it's essence that it can merge with it not only spiritually but also physically resulting a hybrid between the &quot;host&quot; and the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Quite fitting indeed.<br /> <br /> Do they have their own designated sourcebook or are they lumped in with the Mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","name":"Tadpoleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12380_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:01:02-07:00","id":988484,"title":"","content":"They're Astral beings, so detailed in Mage stuff. Like the Astral Realms book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:03:47-07:00","id":988638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987763-how-would-fables-work-in-the-wod-setting?p=988484#post988484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're Astral beings, so detailed in Mage stuff. Like the Astral Realms book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Will have a look at that in due time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12380-tadpoleon","name":"Tadpoleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12380_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T03:20:09-07:00","id":988762,"title":"","content":"Closest Astrals get to their own book is Beast. Which are similar to but not exactly the same as what you're going for here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}